<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45921" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐχθές</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χθές</span>
			, <i>yesterday</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				175
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Th.</u>
				616
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπ᾽ ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					11.35
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Phld.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέσφα τό γ᾽ ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					2.144
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ γάρ τι νῦν γε κἀ</span>.
			today or <i>yesterday</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				456
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἐ. οὐδὲ πρῴην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antipho
					<u>Fr.</u>
					58
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. καὶ τρίτης [ἡμέρας</span>]
				<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ru.</u>
				2.11
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				M.Ant.
				10.7
			</span></i>. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐχθές</span> is commoner than
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χθές</span> in Com. and <i><span class="en">
				LXX
			</span></i>, is the only form used in <u>NT</u>, and freq. in
			papyri of all periods, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PSI</u>
				4.442.21
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, etc.; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χθές</span>.)</div>
